# Resilience (Node.js)

## Retry

- **When:** Transient failures (network, 5xx, 429); not for 4xx (except 429 with backoff)
- **Backoff:** Exponential (e.g. 2^attempt * base); jitter; max attempts and max delay
- **Libraries:** Cockatiel, p-retry, or custom wrapper around promise

## Circuit Breaker

- **States:** Closed (normal); Open (fail fast); Half-Open (probe)
- **Trip:** After N failures in window, open circuit; after timeout, try one request (half-open); close if success
- Use for external services to avoid cascading failure

## Timeout

- Set timeout on outbound HTTP and DB calls; propagate timeout (e.g. request-scoped AbortSignal); return 504 or equivalent when upstream times out

## Bulkhead

- Limit concurrency (e.g. max 10 concurrent calls to service X) to isolate failure; use queue or semaphore

## Conventions

- Retry with backoff for transients; circuit breaker for external deps; timeouts on all I/O; log failures and state changes

## Anti-Patterns

- Retrying 4xx; no timeout; no circuit breaker for flaky services; unbounded concurrency

